From: substrate
Subject: fb: NULL-guard fbBlt against missing-font pixmaps

When the X server's font path doesn't contain a font a client asks
for, XOpenFont can return a "pixmap" whose `bits` is NULL.  The next
attempt to draw with it dives into fbBlt and crashes the server at
0x0 (the NULL src) or 0xc (a NULL+offset deref through one of the
inner-loop macros).

substrate currently ships only libXfont's two builtin fonts
(6x13.builtin + cursor.builtin, with the alias patch mapping `fixed`
to 6x13.builtin).  Clients that request anything else — and many do,
e.g. xterm's resource defaults, matwm2's title bar font — would trip
this every time.

Log once and skip the blit instead of crashing.  Slightly visible
artifacts beat a SIGSEGV.  Once font-misc-misc et al are ported and
in the default path, this guard should hit ~zero in practice but
remains as a safety net.

--- a/fb/fbblt.c
+++ b/fb/fbblt.c
@@ -57,6 +57,23 @@ fbBlt(FbBits * srcLine,
     Bool destInvarient;
     int startbyte, endbyte;

+    /* Substrate hardening: a pixmap with NULL backing storage —
+     * typically an XOpenFont that failed because the requested font
+     * isn't in our (minimal) font path — used to crash this function
+     * with a NULL deref the moment a client tried to draw with it.
+     * Log once and bail instead. */
+    if (!srcLine || !dstLine) {
+        static int warned = 0;
+        if (!warned) {
+            warned = 1;
+            ErrorF("fbBlt: NULL %s drawable (src=%p dst=%p w=%d h=%d bpp=%d) "
+                   "— likely a font/pixmap with no bits; skipping.\n",
+                   !srcLine ? "src" : "dst",
+                   (void *)srcLine, (void *)dstLine, width, height, bpp);
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+
     FbDeclareMergeRop();

     if (alu == GXcopy && pm == FB_ALLONES &&
